one really nice thing about making  biscuits is they are really simple  pretty much you should have everything  in your pantry hi i'm angie and today  i'm going to show you how to make the  flakiest biscuit i'm using biscuit flour  which is predominantly used in the south  you can't really find it sometimes  outside of there so you can just use all  purpose flour so when you get to the  step of adding your butter you want to  make sure that it's very very cold so it  doesn't melt out before you bake them if  you do not have buttermilk you can make  buttermilk take regular whole milk or  even low-fat milk and you can add lemon  juice or white vinegar you want to add  about a half a teaspoon per half cup the  buttermilk adds that nice richness and  flavor so i grew up in north carolina i  definitely grew up eating a hole like  those kids we mainly had them for  breakfast then when i was living my city  life and i didn't have access to  biscuits that i was used to having  that's why i had to learn how to make  them  i like to roll them out fold it over  once fold it over again and then cut  from there and i find that it adds a lot  of layers  when you bake them you definitely want  to have a nice rise if you've done  everything correctly they should double  in size and then you definitely want to  have a nice golden brown on top you  don't want them to get too dark because  once they get too dark they probably are  also going to be a little dry  i'm from the south so i would say with  butter and jelly you can make a sandwich  you can definitely put a piece of fried  chicken which i think is probably the  ultimate way to have it and maybe some  honey  [Music]  let's taste that color  oh yes  [Music]  you
 

